<title>UK: Siebe in deals with Shell, Owens Corning.</title>
<headline>Siebe in deals with Shell, Owens Corning.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Siebe Plc said on Wednesday it had signed global partnership agreements to be the preferred supplier of plant automation solutions to Shell International B.V. and Owens Corning.</p>
<p>Siebe's controls systems division will provide computer-based plant automation systems, field instrumentation and control valves to Shell and Owens Corning plants world-wide.</p>
<p>The agreement with Shell is designed to reduce the cost of ownership of plant automation systems by 25 percent over the next four years.</p>
<p>The agreement covers all Shell International-operated firms around the world.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
